<?php
/**
 * Spartrak Login/Register Modal.
 *
 * FIGMA-MEASURED REBUILD, 2026-08-26. The Figma MCP connector is now
 * authorized, so the "SCOPE, still open: exact Figma spacing/typography/icons
 * for every step (BLOCKED / REQUIRES FIGMA ACCESS)" note this docblock used to
 * carry is resolved. Source nodes, desktop then mobile:
 *
 *   login              561:9925   /  688:22943
 *   register - phone   569:10235  /  688:23851
 *   OTP                561:10625  /  688:23390   (+ disabled + complete states)
 *   register - details  569:12394  /  688:25218
 *   loading            572:15113  /  688:25653
 *
 * The MARKUP changed shape in three ways as a result, all of them structural
 * rather than cosmetic; see _login-modal.less for the measured values.
 *
 *  1. Every step now has a HEADING BLOCK — a 28px title plus a muted 16px
 *     lede — where before it had a bare 20px title. Figma writes a specific
 *     description for each of the five states; none of them was rendered.
 *
 *  2. The OTP step is a different component, not a restyled one. It echoes the
 *     number back inside a 12px-radius chip with a 24x24 phone icon, and its
 *     four cells are 72x80 with a 32px digit over a 24px underline. The
 *     `placeholder=" "` on each cell is load-bearing, not decoration: it makes
 *     the not-yet-filled state addressable as `:placeholder-shown` so the
 *     lighter underline Figma exports for an empty cell needs no JS class.
 *
 *  3. "Or continue with" is a bare centred line of text. The two hairlines
 *     that used to flank it exist in no Figma state.
 *
 * WHERE THIS DELIBERATELY DIVERGES FROM FIGMA, and why. Each of these is a
 * conflict inside the design source or with a settled business rule, not a
 * preference:
 *
 *  a. THE MOBILE LOGIN STEP IS PHONE-ONLY IN FIGMA (no password field; its CTA
 *     is "التالي", implying phone -> OTP -> in). The desktop login node has
 *     phone AND password. The settled business rule is phone + password signs
 *     in directly, with OTP reserved for signup and password reset — so the
 *     desktop node is the one implemented, at the mobile node's panel
 *     geometry. CLAUDE.md §3: Figma wins on presentation, not against an
 *     explicit business requirement.
 *
 *  b. THE DESKTOP LOGIN CTA READS "التالي" ("Next") even though that step has
 *     both fields and completes the journey. That label is inherited from the
 *     phone-first mobile flow in (a). Rendered as "Sign in" — which is Figma's
 *     own string for this action on the OTP-login state ("تسجيل الدخول").
 *
 *  c. NO FORGOT-PASSWORD FLOW EXISTS IN FIGMA. The backend has supported
 *     `purpose=password_reset` end to end (send -> verify -> resetPost) all
 *     along, and dropping the entry point would leave a shopper who forgot
 *     their password with no route back into their account. The three reset
 *     steps are kept and built from the SAME measured components as the Figma
 *     states — no new visual language is invented for them.
 *
 *  d. NO CLOSE BUTTON EXISTS IN ANY OF THE FOURTEEN FIGMA STATES. One is kept:
 *     a modal dialog must expose a visible, focusable dismiss control
 *     (CLAUDE.md §15). Esc and a scrim click are both undiscoverable and
 *     neither is announced to assistive tech.
 *
 *  e. FIGMA COPY TYPOS are corrected, and listed here so the correction is
 *     reviewable rather than silent: the OTP title reads "أدخل رمز OPT" (OPT
 *     for OTP) in all four OTP states; the loading title reads "لحظه من فضلك"
 *     (لحظه for لحظة); the details labels read "الأسم" (for الاسم). The
 *     corrected forms are in i18n/ar_EG.csv.
 *
 *  f. THE COUNTRY FLAG IS NOT RENDERED — BLOCKED / REQUIRES FIGMA ASSET. The
 *     20x20 flag beside "+20" cannot be exported cleanly (it is ~28 vector
 *     fragments inside a component variant, and every export returns either
 *     the fragments or a canvas-contaminated render), and the one clean export
 *     that reached this repo is the SYRIAN flag — Figma's variant for this
 *     instance is labelled `Property = syria`, which is a defect in the design
 *     file for an Egypt-only store. A wrong national flag is worse than none,
 *     and authoring or downloading a substitute is forbidden (CLAUDE.md §3).
 *     See the note in _login-modal.less for exactly what to add when the
 *     correct asset lands.
 *
 * UNCHANGED FROM THE PREVIOUS BUILD, and still true:
 *
 *  - REGISTRATION FIELD SET: mobile -> OTP -> firstname + lastname + password
 *    + confirmation. No email field, ever — `Registrar::register()` does not
 *    accept one as a parameter, so a posted `email` could not reach account
 *    identity even by accident. The backend synthesizes an internal
 *    placeholder address (PlaceholderEmail / CustomerEmail view model); it is
 *    never rendered anywhere customer-facing. `password_confirmation` is
 *    REQUIRED server-side (CreatePost.php).
 *
 *  - THE OTP BOX COUNT IS CONFIGURATION, NOT A CONSTANT. It renders
 *    `code_length` cells. Figma draws 4 and the shipped default is now 4, but
 *    the range is admin-settable 4-8 and hardcoding 4 would leave a shopper
 *    unable to type digits 5 and 6 of a code they can see in the SMS. The
 *    stylesheet caps each cell at Figma's 72px and lets them shrink, so a
 *    longer code still fits one line on a phone.
 *
 *  - NO FORM KEY IS RENDERED. This block is cacheable and store-scoped on
 *    purpose, and a form key baked into a cached page is stale for everyone
 *    who receives it. The widget reads the `form_key` cookie and rewrites it
 *    from each auth response — sign-in, registration and reset all regenerate
 *    the session id, invalidating the previous key. See spartrak-auth.js.
 *
 *  - GOOGLE IS INERT: rendered per Figma, but `disabled`, with no handler and
 *    no data-auth-* hook. Social login is not part of this build; the control
 *    exists so the layout matches the design without silently dropping a
 *    Figma element and without building unrequested OAuth.
 *
 * Per-field errors: a server error whose response carries a `field` key
 * (FieldValidationException / InvalidPhoneNumberException — see
 * AbstractJsonAction) is rendered against the matching `[data-field-error]`
 * element inside the submitting form, in addition to — not instead of — the
 * shared `[data-auth-error]` region, which still carries the message text for
 * screen readers and for any error with no specific field.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 * @var \Spartrak\CustomerAuth\ViewModel\AuthConfig $authConfig
 */

$authConfig = $block->getData('auth_config');

$codeLength = $authConfig->getCodeLength();
$signupPurpose = $authConfig->getSignupPurpose();
$resetPurpose = $authConfig->getPasswordResetPurpose();
$countryCode = $authConfig->getDefaultCountryCode();
$ttlMinutes = $authConfig->getCodeTtlMinutes();

$widgetConfig = [
    'spartrakAuth' => [
        'endpoints' => [
            'otpSend' => $block->getUrl('spartrak_auth/otp/send', ['_secure' => true]),
            'otpVerify' => $block->getUrl('spartrak_auth/otp/verify', ['_secure' => true]),
            'login' => $block->getUrl('spartrak_auth/account/loginPost', ['_secure' => true]),
            'register' => $block->getUrl('spartrak_auth/account/createPost', ['_secure' => true]),
            'passwordReset' => $block->getUrl('spartrak_auth/password/resetPost', ['_secure' => true]),
        ],
        'codeLength' => $codeLength,
        'resendSeconds' => $authConfig->getResendCooldownSeconds(),
    ],
];

/**
 * The heading block every step opens with: 28px title + muted 16px lede,
 * centred, 12px apart (Figma "Tittle and Description", 561:9926).
 *
 * `$measure` reflects Figma's own per-state choice rather than a default:
 * login and both OTP steps cap the lede at 264px so it breaks into the
 * balanced lines the design shows, while the register steps let it run the
 * full content width.
 */
$head = static function (
    string $stepId,
    string $title,
    string $lede,
    bool $measure = false
) use ($block): string {
    $ledeClass = 'spartrak-auth__lede' . ($measure ? ' spartrak-auth__lede--measure' : '');

    return '<div class="spartrak-auth__head">'
        . '<h2 class="spartrak-auth__title" id="spartrak-auth-title-' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($stepId) . '">'
        . $block->escapeHtml($title)
        . '</h2>'
        . '<p class="' . $ledeClass . '">' . $block->escapeHtml($lede) . '</p>'
        . '</div>';
};

/**
 * Per-step error region. `role="alert"` so a screen reader announces a failed
 * sign-in without the shopper having to go looking for it, and `hidden` rather
 * than empty so an emptied region is not announced as a change.
 *
 * Hidden means `display: none`, so it contributes no flex gap while there is
 * no message — the step's spacing is Figma's exactly until something goes
 * wrong, and only then does the region take its place in the rhythm.
 */
$errorRegion = static function (): string {
    return '<p class="spartrak-auth__error" data-auth-error role="alert" hidden></p>';
};

/**
 * Per-field error slot. Empty and hidden until spartrak-auth.js fills one in
 * from a response's `field` key.
 *
 * `role="alert"` added 2026-08-27, when _showError stopped mirroring every
 * field message into the shared region as well (it was printing each one
 * twice). The shared region used to be the only live region on the step, so
 * with the message now landing HERE instead, this element has to announce it
 * — otherwise de-duplicating the visible text would have silently cost screen
 * reader users the announcement entirely.
 */
$fieldError = static function (string $field) use ($block): string {
    return '<span class="spartrak-auth__field-error" data-field-error="'
        . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($field) . '" role="alert" hidden></span>';
};

/**
 * The phone field: a 48px bordered wrapper holding the entry segment and a
 * "+NN" country chip.
 *
 * FIGMA SSOT: node 817:19277 ("Text Input"), re-read 2026-08-27 — Inputs
 * wrapper h48 / border 1px border/default / radius 0 / Shadow-Input; chip
 * padding 12 (near) 14 (far), gap 8, children [ "+NN" 16px Medium, flag 20 ],
 * divider on the chip's far edge; entry segment flex-1, padding 8/12,
 * placeholder in text/muted.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * CHIP ORDER — FIXED 2026-08-27
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The chip used to be emitted FIRST, which in this RTL document put it at the
 * right-hand end of the field. Figma's own render of this component (the frame
 * is the Arabic one) puts the chip at the LEFT and the number entry to its
 * right, with the hairline divider between them. Emitting the chip LAST is
 * what reproduces that, and it follows the same "reverse Figma's LTR child
 * order" rule the rest of this header/modal pass already uses (see
 * mobile-nav-drawer.phtml and _support-strip.less).
 *
 * Tab order is unaffected: the chip is an aria-hidden <span>, not a control,
 * so the field still receives focus directly.
 *
 * The chip is display context ONLY — aria-hidden, and never concatenated with
 * the value before posting. The server-side Normalizer applies the default
 * country code itself and accepts a local "01…" number, so prepending "+20"
 * here would produce "+2001…" and fail every submission.
 *
 * The flag is Figma's own 20x20 glyph for this component
 * (images/icons/phone-country-flag.svg) — see that file's usage note in
 * _login-modal.less, which records what the glyph actually depicts.
 */
$phoneField = static function (
    string $id,
    string $label,
    string $placeholder
) use ($block, $fieldError, $countryCode): string {
    $flagUrl = $block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/icons/phone-country-flag.svg'));

    return '<div class="field required">'
        . '<label for="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) . '">' . $block->escapeHtml($label) . '</label>'
        . '<div class="spartrak-auth__phone">'
        . '<input type="tel" id="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) . '" name="phone" class="input-text" '
        . 'placeholder="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($placeholder) . '" '
        . 'data-auth-phone-input required autocomplete="tel" inputmode="tel" />'
        . '<span class="spartrak-auth__phone-code" aria-hidden="true">'
        . '<span class="spartrak-auth__phone-code-value">+' . $block->escapeHtml($countryCode) . '</span>'
        . '<img class="spartrak-auth__phone-flag" src="' . $flagUrl . '" width="20" height="20" alt="" '
        . 'aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />'
        . '</span>'
        . '</div>'
        . $fieldError('phone')
        . '</div>';
};

/**
 * A password field with Figma's eye reveal.
 *
 * One closure rather than repeating this markup at all five password inputs
 * (login, registration x2, reset x2): a shared render point means the reveal
 * can never drift out of sync between fields the way five hand-copied blocks
 * eventually would.
 *
 * The reveal is a real flex sibling of the input, ordered AFTER it, which puts
 * it at the inline-end — Figma's position — and gives the natural tab order
 * (into the field, then onto its own control). It is working JS
 * (spartrak-auth.js `_onPasswordToggle`): it flips type="password" <-> "text"
 * and updates aria-pressed/aria-label. The glyph itself does not change,
 * because only one eye icon exists in the design; inventing a second "hidden"
 * variant is exactly the asset guess CLAUDE.md §3 forbids.
 */
$passwordField = static function (
    string $id,
    string $name,
    string $label,
    string $placeholder,
    string $autocomplete
) use ($block, $fieldError): string {
    $eyeIconUrl = $block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/icons/password-eye.svg'));

    return '<div class="field required">'
        . '<label for="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) . '">' . $block->escapeHtml($label) . '</label>'
        . '<div class="spartrak-auth__password">'
        . '<input type="password" id="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) . '" '
        . 'name="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($name) . '" class="input-text" '
        . 'placeholder="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($placeholder) . '" '
        . 'required autocomplete="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($autocomplete) . '" />'
        . '<button type="button" class="spartrak-auth__reveal" data-password-toggle '
        . 'aria-pressed="false" aria-label="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Show password')) . '" '
        . 'aria-controls="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) . '">'
        . '<img src="' . $eyeIconUrl . '" width="20" height="20" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />'
        . '</button>'
        . '</div>'
        . $fieldError($name === 'password_confirmation' ? 'password_confirmation' : 'password')
        . '</div>';
};

/**
 * The number being verified, echoed back in Figma's 12px-radius chip with its
 * 24x24 phone icon. Filled by spartrak-auth.js from the send response.
 */
$phoneChip = static function () use ($block): string {
    $iconUrl = $block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/icons/phone-call.svg'));

    return '<p class="spartrak-auth__phone-chip">'
        . '<img src="' . $iconUrl . '" width="24" height="24" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />'
        . '<span class="spartrak-auth__phone-echo" data-auth-phone-echo></span>'
        . '</p>';
};

/**
 * One OTP entry group, rendered per verify step.
 *
 * Each step gets its own group rather than sharing one: the signup and reset
 * journeys are separate step machines, and a shared group would carry digits
 * typed in one flow into the other when a shopper backs out and starts again.
 *
 * The `placeholder=" "` attribute was dropped on 2026-08-27 along with the
 * `:placeholder-shown` rule it existed to trigger. Figma draws only two cell
 * states — filled (rule in icon/default) and active (border AND rule in
 * action/primary) — so the third, "empty but not focused, lighter rule" state
 * that rule invented is gone, and with it the attribute's only consumer.
 */
$otpGroup = static function (string $stepId) use ($block, $codeLength): string {
    $html = '<div class="spartrak-otp" data-otp-group role="group" aria-label="'
        . $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Verification code')) . '">';

    for ($i = 0; $i < $codeLength; $i++) {
        $html .= '<input type="text" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="1" '
            . 'autocomplete="' . ($i === 0 ? 'one-time-code' : 'off') . '" '
            . 'class="spartrak-otp__box" data-otp-box '
            . 'id="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr($stepId . '-otp-' . $i) . '" '
            . 'aria-label="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Digit %1', $i + 1)) . '" />';
    }

    return $html . '</div>';
};

/**
 * The resend control. Figma renders it as a full-width grey button with no
 * countdown; the countdown span is a Spartrak addition, because the backend
 * enforces a cooldown and a button that silently rejects a click for 60
 * seconds is worse than one that says why. `data-resend-seconds` is only the
 * pre-first-response value; each send response carries an authoritative
 * `resend_in`.
 */
$resendControl = static function () use ($block, $authConfig): string {
    return '<button type="button" class="spartrak-auth__secondary" data-otp-resend disabled '
        . 'data-resend-seconds="' . (int) $authConfig->getResendCooldownSeconds() . '">'
        . '<span data-resend-label>' . $block->escapeHtml(__('Resend code')) . '</span>'
        . ' <span class="spartrak-auth__resend-timer" data-resend-countdown>('
        . '<span data-resend-timer>' . (int) $authConfig->getResendCooldownSeconds() . '</span>s)</span>'
        . '</button>';
};

/** Bare centred line. NO flanking rules — see the class docblock. */
$orText = static function () use ($block): string {
    return '<p class="spartrak-auth__or">' . $block->escapeHtml(__('Or continue with')) . '</p>';
};

/**
 * Deliberately NOT a <button type="submit"> and NOT inside data-auth-form's
 * submit handling: `disabled` makes it inert to both click and keyboard
 * activation, and it carries no data-auth-* attribute to bind to.
 *
 * Icon before label in DOM, which lands it on Figma's side of the centred pair
 * in RTL and mirrors correctly in LTR without an override.
 */
$googleButton = static function () use ($block): string {
    $iconUrl = $block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/icons/google.svg'));

    return '<button type="button" class="spartrak-auth__social" disabled '
        . 'title="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Coming soon')) . '" '
        . 'aria-label="' . $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Continue with Google')) . '">'
        . '<img src="' . $iconUrl . '" width="20" height="20" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />'
        . '<span>' . $block->escapeHtml(__('Continue with Google')) . '</span>'
        . '</button>';
};
